y.","marking_guide":"Accept a named misconception about elapsed, corrected working, and a method reason. Reject vague “I was wrong” with no repair.","question":"Describe one likely mistake with elapsed, show corrected working, and say why the correction works.","sample_answer":"Sample misconception: Subtracting digital times as if they were base-100 decimals (e.g.. Correction uses 1 hour 35 minutes.. Why: restores accurate elapsed.","type":"short_answer"}],"resources":null,"response_prompt":"Include your independent working and reflection, with reasons where requested.","review_status":"unreviewed","seed_key":"s2-mat-y4-w30-l1","sort_activity":null,"source_note":"Proposed Stage 2 NESA mathematics alignment using verified outcome code wording where recorded in lesson-pipeline/sources; content-point mapping remains pending.","spelling":null,"spelling_focus":null,"stage":"S2","stage_hints":{"accept":["Today you will practise elapsed.","Read the mission before you start calculating.","Keep the place or unit you are working with in view."],"guided":["Attempt the guided prompt without looking ahead.","Afterwards, compare your working with the feedback.","Adjust anything that does not match the method."],"learn":["Study how the first demonstration is built.","Point to the place or distance that carries the method.","Then write the reason without copying every sentence."],"quiz":["Read every option before you choose.","Eliminate answers that ignore place value or working.","Prefer accurate method over a guess that merely looks neat."],"submit":["Confirm that your working and reason are both present.","Proofread digits, places and operation signs.","Make sure the final evidence matches the lesson purpose."],"teach0":["Read the stage title and find the worked model.","Name one exact place, value or distance before you decide.","Try the small prompt before opening the comparison."],"teach1":["Return to the model and list the key numbers.","Say what each number represents in the method.","A final answer alone is weaker than labelled working."],"teach2":["Compare a weak attempt with stronger working.","Change the value or method, not only how neat it looks.","Name the mistake you are repairing."],"teach3":["Choose fresh numbers that still use the same skill.","Write one reason in your own words.","Do not retype the worked model as your answer."],"write":["Follow every part of the independent instructions.","Include original working and a short reason.","Save work that shows the skill on new numbers."]},"subject":"Measurement and Space","success_criteria":["I can use elapsed with a specific example from this lesson.","I can identify duration and explain why it matters.","I can practise start independently on a new prompt.","I can notice end needs and correct a likely mistake."],"suspense_builder":null,"teach_steps":[{"check":{"correct_index":1,"explanation":"Elapsed time is the duration from a start time to an end time; jump hours then minutes on a number line or clock. Supported working follows the actual numbers and purpose of the task. Apply the lesson idea with evidence. The other choices miss a key step or use a common mistake.","options":["An answer copied without understanding","Elapsed time is the duration from a start time to an end time","A guess with no working","A calculation unrelated to the numbers given"],"question":"Which choice best applies this lesson idea about elapsed with clear evidence?","type":"multiple_choice"},"example":"WORKED MODEL\nStart 9:20, end 11:05 → +1 h to 10:20 +45 min to 11:05 = 1 h 45 min. Crossing noon needs am/pm or 24-hour care.\n\nTRY FIRST\nHow much time from 2:40 pm to 4:15 pm?\n\nFEEDBACK\n1 hour 35 minutes.","explain":"Elapsed time is the duration from a start time to an end time; jump hours then minutes on a number line or clock.\n\nWHY IT MATTERS\nThis helps the learner choose methods based on place value, quantity and accurate working, rather than guessing digits by shape alone. Keep every step justified.\n\nHOW TO WORK\nRead the worked example and name the places, values or distances that carry the method. Before looking at the correction, make your own attempt using the exact question provided. Compare your working with the feedback: did you use the same skill and show your reasoning? If a digit or place is uncertain, identify what would have to be regrouped or counted again. One deliberate, justified revision is more useful than writing a longer answer.","icon":"📖","notice":"Subtracting digital times as if they were base-100 decimals (e.g. 4.15−2.40) fails when minutes borrow. Correct the value or method, not just the appearance of the digits.","title":"Understand and model","visual":[{"alt":"Elapsed time method.","caption":"Not base-100 decimal subtract.","svg":"<svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" viewBox=\"0 0 660 150\"><rect x=\"10\" y=\"12\" width=\"310\" height=\"126\" rx=\"14\" fill=\"#fff4ea\" stroke=\"#b87445\"/><rect x=\"340\" y=\"12\" width=\"310\" height=\"126\" rx=\"14\" fill=\"#e8f5ed\" stroke=\"#297a61\"/><g font-size=\"16\" fill=\"#263948\"><text x=\"28\" y=\"42\">Jump hours</text><text x=\"28\" y=\"78\">then minutes</text><text x=\"358\" y=\"42\">Elapsed</text><text x=\"358\" y=\"78\">duration</text></g></svg>"}],"visual_before":[{"episode":{"scenes":[{"bg":"room","lines":[{"text":"I can see the example, but I am not sure which number or place matters most.","who":"pip"},{"text":"Name the places, values or distances that carry the method before you decide.","who":"juno"},{"text":"I will try the prompt myself, then compare with the feedback.","who":"pip"},{"pause_after":true,"text":"Pause here. Use this model: Start 9:20, end 11:05 → +1 h to 10:20 +45 min to 11:05 = 1 h 45 min. Crossing noon needs am/pm or 24-hour care. Then write your own working.","who":"juno"}]}],"title":"Talk through the first model","transcript":"Pip: I can see the example, but I am not sure which number or place matters most.\nJuno: Name the places, values 